This repo is used to store my configuration files on Linux (and macOS).

Dotfiles *and* the tools they depend on are managed with chezmoi
(https://www.chezmoi.io/): one `chezmoi apply` sets up a whole machine.

Layout
------
  .chezmoiroot          tells chezmoi the source state lives in home/
  home/                 chezmoi source state (mirrors $HOME)
    .chezmoi.toml.tmpl    per-machine config; asks once which optional
                          components to install (AI agents, Docker, Tailscale)
    .chezmoidata/packages.yaml
                          package lists (apt, brew, uv tools, npm globals)
    .chezmoiexternal.toml.tmpl
                          single-binary tools from GitHub releases into
                          ~/.local/bin: lazygit, delta, difft, uv/uvx
    .chezmoiscripts/      install scripts, re-run when their inputs change:
      run_onchange_before_10-install-system-packages   apt / brew
      run_onchange_after_20-install-uv-tools           mdformat, ...
      run_onchange_after_30-install-ai-agents          nvm+node, claude, codex, gemini, opencode
      run_onchange_after_40-install-docker             if docker = true (Linux)
      run_onchange_after_50-install-tailscale          if tailscale = true
      run_onchange_after_fix-terminal-paste            bracketed-paste fix
    dot_bashrc            -> ~/.bashrc  (dot_ = leading ".")
    create_dot_bash_exports -> ~/.bash_exports, only created if missing
                             (put machine-local exports/secrets here)
    modify_dot_gitconfig.tmpl -> ~/.gitconfig, merged via update_gitconfig.py
                             so the machine's [user]/[credential] sections stay
    dot_config/nvim/      -> ~/.config/nvim/init.vim (= .vimrc)
    dot_config/kitty/     -> ~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf (only if kitty exists)
    dot_local/bin/        -> ~/.local/bin (runwlog, ...)
  .gitconfig            base git config consumed by update_gitconfig.py
  install_agents_jails.py  optional, run by hand: sandbox AI agent configs

First-time setup on a new machine
---------------------------------
  sh -c "$(curl -fsLS get.chezmoi.io)" -- -b ~/.local/bin init --apply nedn/dotfiles

or, from an existing clone:

  git clone https://github.com/nedn/dotfiles ~/projects/dotfiles
  ~/projects/dotfiles/setup_dot.sh     # installs chezmoi if needed, then applies

chezmoi asks which optional components this machine wants; answers are saved
in ~/.config/chezmoi/chezmoi.toml. Change them later with
`chezmoi init --prompt && chezmoi apply`.

Set GITHUB_TOKEN to avoid GitHub API rate limits when resolving the latest
releases in .chezmoiexternal.toml.tmpl.

Adding a tool
-------------
  apt/brew/uv/npm package   add it to home/.chezmoidata/packages.yaml
  GitHub release binary     add an entry to home/.chezmoiexternal.toml.tmpl
  anything else             add a run_onchange_ script to home/.chezmoiscripts/
Then `chezmoi apply` on each machine (after `git pull`, or `chezmoi update`).

Day to day
----------
  chezmoi update               # git pull + apply
  chezmoi diff                 # preview what would change in $HOME
  chezmoi apply                # apply the repo to $HOME (and install tools)
  chezmoi edit --apply ~/.bashrc
  chezmoi re-add ~/.bashrc     # pull edits made directly in $HOME back into the repo
  chezmoi cd                   # open a shell in this repo
